      "original_record": "before",
      "value": "Which of the following statements are true regarding the function given below?\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}-x+4, & x<1 \\\\ 0, & x=1 \\\\ x+2, & x>1\\end{aligned}\\,\n$$\n\nI. It is continuous and differentiable at $x=1$\n\nII. It is differentiable on the interval $(-2,2)$\n\nIII. It is **not** differentiable at $x=1$",
